    <briefdescription>
<para>Deprecated comparison and logical operators of the test checks. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1operators" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::operators</ref></computeroutput> namespace provides the deprecated overloaded operators of the test checks.</para>
<para>This namespace includes the equality, inequality, relational, and logical operators of the framework expression types, which apply to the strongly-typed constants (the user-defined literals) and to the dynamic values (the wrappers).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>These operators may conflict with other operators defined within the application under test.</para>
</simplesect>
To minimise conflicts with application-defined operators, these overloads are enabled only when an operand is a framework expression type (see <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1is__op" kindref="compound">extension::is_op</ref></computeroutput>). Constants typically require a literal suffix (e.g., <computeroutput>1<ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1ga8468610e763177a8f569f7d618851288" kindref="member">_i</ref></computeroutput>), while dynamic values should be wrapped using the provided casting utilities (e.g., <computeroutput>mt::to_i{...}</computeroutput>). When neither operand is of such a type, the standard operators are selected; they return a plain <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, so a failed check cannot show the operands.</para>
<para>The operands are forwarded, as by the function comparators: the temporaries are moved into the returned expression, and the named operands are copied, unless they cannot be copied, when they are referred to.</para>
<para>There are no operators for strings and containers: the standard operators would be selected for <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> objects and for containers of the same type, and the framework operators for <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> objects would also replace the standard ones in the application code that follows the using directive. Use <computeroutput>mt::eq()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>mt::ne()</computeroutput> to compare strings and containers.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Deprecated</title><para>Use the function comparators <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga0fbc0f7ddf0107c1e5265bb79287487d" kindref="member">eq()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga92cdc2dde6af040f2f5f5df677df0985" kindref="member">ne()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga90da2cbc14b4562332a205d5b232356f" kindref="member">gt()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga58c7dacabca3fe1b0dc025a0e0f30e9e" kindref="member">ge()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga493a42c738ef38b45a28b06a2155aa00" kindref="member">lt()</ref></computeroutput>, and <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-function-comparators_1ga9125d2dd997269eecc0d8239d5df67e5" kindref="member">le()</ref></computeroutput>, with the plain values, and <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-logical-functions_1ga0a385c59a2f7d3c4cfef77d2d3b4f3d6" kindref="member">all_of()</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-logical-functions_1gadc2224d07a9bf118c8772518a7d3c4fd" kindref="member">any_of()</ref></computeroutput>, and <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-logical-functions_1gae82d39ac86167bb4bfa6624676f3729e" kindref="member">negate()</ref></computeroutput> for the logical combinations (since 6.0.0). The function comparators accept the same operands, compare them and report them in the same way, and do not need the literal suffixes or the type wrappers.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="since"><para>3.2.0 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
